y the observed outcomes.\\\"],\\\"preferences\\\":[],\\\"projects\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"multi-wrap-lashing-study\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"active\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"Can a continuous handmade reed cord fit and retain a two-turn lashing of my two branch pieces?\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"At tick 335 the 0.54 m cord failed the measured two-turn length requirement of 0.6273 m.\\\",\\\"At tick 343 the sectioned-cord operation completed a cord with 0.60 m twisted length and 0.64 m overall length.\\\",\\\"At tick 350 the two-turn lashing of the two 31.6 mm branches passed its release check. Recorded maximum stage need was 0.6124 m, with two 0.0538 m tails.\\\"],\\\"uncertainty\\\":\\\"Fit and release retention are established for these actual items; load behavior and durability remain untested.\\\",\\\"goal\\\":\\\"Establish actual two-turn fit and measure limited separation and sliding load behavior.\\\",\\\"completedSteps\\\":[\\\"Learned the multi-turn lashing method.\\\",\\\"Measured the original cord's shortfall.\\\",\\\"Made the longer continuous cord.\\\",\\\"Completed and released the two-turn lashing.\\\"],\\\"outputs\\\":[\\\"Bound assembly lashing-346-wren-3982.\\\",\\\"Observed successful fit and unloaded retention of the 0.64 m cord.\\\"],\\\"missing\\\":\\\"Measured separation and sliding trials.\\\",\\\"next\\\":\\\"Test 5 N separation for 10 seconds and 1 N sliding for 10 seconds, then review measured displacement, damage and retention.\\\",\\\"pauseReason\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"benefit\\\":\\\"The longer cord physically completed the two-turn closure that the earlier cord could not fit.\\\"}],\\\"cares\\\":null,\\\"views\\\":{}}\"}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":true,"prompt_cache_key":"7e5d0e63-a81a-4395-a2a4-eabd147c12e8","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"json_schema","name":"bounded_decision","description":null,"sche